Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-18 (2026-08-15)
------------------------------------

- Made the native desktop New menu independent from the filer New/Templates
  menu. The desktop now offers only Directory, File and Launcher.
- Added a native GTK3 launcher editor that creates a .desktop file in ~/Desktop
  with configurable Name, Command and Icon fields.
- Added a command chooser that starts in /usr/bin and an icon chooser that
  starts in /usr/share/pixmaps; both can browse anywhere in the filesystem.
- Newly created launchers are made executable and are immediately picked up by
  the existing Rox-Filer2 desktop launcher code.
- Added the new Launcher label to all 13 actively maintained translations and
  regenerated their GNU gettext .mo catalogues.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-17 (2026-08-15)
------------------------------------

- Fixed the GTK3 Wayland activation popover callback: GtkMenuButton returns a
  GtkPopover pointer, which is now handled with the correct type.
- Removed two unused native-desktop helper functions left by the 2.12.2-15
  selection/placement work, eliminating the corresponding compiler warnings.
- No new user-visible strings were added; existing translations remain valid.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-16 (2026-08-15)
====================================
- Fixed the Wayland single/double-click selector so the GtkPopover contents are
  visible when the anchored menu button opens.
- Fixed the desktop New/Templates submenu so its synthetic desktop target no
  longer overwrites the global active filer window. New directory, blank-file
  and template saveboxes now remember only a real filer window for autoselect.
- Made X11 IPC recovery safe: if an existing valid ROX IPC owner does not reply,
  the current request continues locally without deleting the owner's root
  property or stealing primary-instance ownership.
- Fixed a GdkWindow reference leak when an advertised IPC window fails its
  self-property validation.
- Desktop drag-and-drop now accepts sources that offer COPY as well as LINK,
  while still creating a symbolic link in ~/Desktop and never moving the
  original object.
- Fixed a small template-menu path leak for duplicate template entries.
- Updated current translation/template metadata to 2.12.2-16; no new
  user-visible strings were added.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-15 (2026-08-13)
====================================
- Added rubber-band selection to the native desktop. Dragging on empty desktop
  space now selects multiple icons with the mouse; Ctrl/Shift extends the
  existing selection. Selected icons can already be dragged together and are
  now also handled together by the desktop file actions.
- Expanded the desktop item context menu with Cut, Copy and Rename while
  keeping Move to Trash multi-selection aware.
- Added the same New/Templates submenu used by filer windows to the desktop
  background context menu.
- Added drag-and-drop from filer windows to the native desktop. Local files and
  folders are pinned by creating symbolic links in ~/Desktop, preserving the
  original object instead of moving or duplicating it.
- Fixed a stale X11 IPC handle that could make `roxfiler` with no parameters
  report that an existing Rox-Filer2 process was not responding. A stale owner
  is now discarded and the request continues locally.
- Replaced the Desktop Preferences single/double-click GtkComboBox popup with
  an anchored GtkMenuButton + GtkPopover, fixing the detached/far-away popup
  reported on Wayland.
- Added translations for the new desktop drag-and-drop error messages to all
  13 actively maintained Rox-Filer2 locales.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-14 (2026-08-13)

- Fixed the toolbar overflow menu for New. When the toolbar becomes too narrow,
  the overflow entry now remains a real submenu ("New >") instead of becoming
  a flat menu item.
- The overflow New entry reuses create_menu_new(), so Directory, Blank file,
  Customise Menu and templates are identical to the normal New menu.
- The New icon keeps the fixed GTK menu-size slot introduced in 2.12.2-12, so
  the plus icon stays aligned with Search, Trash and the other overflow items.
- No GIF files were added; native GTK3 progress indicators from 2.12.2-13 are
  preserved.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-13 (2026-08-13)
====================================
- Removed the bundled operation GIF files. Copy, Move and Delete now use a
  native GTK3 GtkSpinner plus GtkProgressBar. The bar pulses when progress is
  unknown and switches to the real percentage when ROX reports one.
- Operation dialogs keep the compact Details/Show Log behaviour and use only
  existing gettext strings, so all 13 maintained Rox-Filer2 locales remain
  covered without adding untranslated UI text.
- Restored New as a real GTK3 menu/submenu button on the toolbar. The same +
  opens the New menu, and its drop-down uses the same Directory, Blank file,
  Customise Menu and Templates content as the context-menu New submenu.
- The context-menu New entry remains an actual <Branch> submenu and keeps the
  GTK_ICON_SIZE_MENU alignment fix from 2.12.2-12.
- The source archive contains no .gif files; README now uses the existing PNG
  desktop screenshot.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-12 (2026-08-13)
====================================
- GTK3 menu alignment: the New submenu now uses the standard list-add icon.
- Normalised themed menu icons to GTK_ICON_SIZE_MENU and vertically centred
  menu content so New aligns with Search, Trash and the other menu rows.
- No custom image assets were added.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-11 (2026-08-13)
-----------------------------------
* Toolbar customisation: replaced the slow Up/Down controls with a numeric
  Position field. Partitions remains fixed at position 1; assigning a new
  number moves the selected button directly and renumbers the others.
* Toolbar visibility remains unchanged: enabled buttons are shown and hidden
  buttons keep their saved place in the order.
* Browser and Console commands now read the last saved shared Options value at
  launch time, so changes take effect immediately after pressing OK even when
  Rox-Filer2 --desktop is a separate long-running process. No restart is
  required.
* Updated translations for the new toolbar, browser/console, video-thumbnail
  and audio-preview interface strings.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-10 (2026-08-13)

- Toolbar options now keep the existing show/hide behaviour and add explicit
  Up/Down controls so users can rearrange toolbar buttons live.
- Partitions remains permanent and fixed in the first toolbar position; it is
  shown as a fixed row in the customiser and cannot be hidden or moved.
- Toolbar order is saved in the new `toolbar_order` option and restored across
  sessions; unknown/new tools fall back safely to the built-in order.
- The + button is now a normal single toolbar button. Clicking the + itself
  opens the exact New menu anchored directly below it, with no split-arrow and
  no separate popup GUI.
- The + menu continues to share Directory, Blank file, Customise Menu and the
  same user/bundled Templates entries as the context-menu New submenu.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-9 (2026-08-13)

- Toolbar: clicking the + (New) button now opens the complete New menu instead
  of immediately creating a directory. It matches the context-menu New submenu.
- Toolbar: the New drop-down uses the same ordering as the context menu:
  Directory, Blank file, Customise Menu, then user/bundled templates.
- Toolbar: Search now uses the standard GTK3 icon name `edit-find` through
  `ROX_ICON_FIND`, so it follows the active GTK icon theme.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-8 (2026-08-13)

- Fixes video thumbnails not appearing: ffmpeg now writes a temporary frame,
  then Rox-Filer2 saves it through its normal thumbnail writer so the cached
  PNG contains the required Freedesktop Thumb::MTime/Size/URI metadata.
- Automatically removes invalid metadata-less video thumbnails produced by
  2.12.2-6/7 and regenerates them when needed.
- Thumbnail cache purge no longer opens the old normal file-delete dialog.
  It directly clears ~/.cache/thumbnails/normal (and legacy
  ~/.thumbnails/normal when present), purges the in-memory cache and refreshes
  filer windows.
- Cache purge no longer creates an empty cache directory just to delete it.
- Audio preview now follows Puppy's real run-as-spot wrapper directly: if
  run-as-spot exists it is used; otherwise mpv is launched normally. The
  wrapper itself handles root-versus-normal-user behaviour.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-7 (2026-08-13)

- Puppy-aware audio preview: when Rox-Filer2 is running as root on Puppy
  (detected by /etc/DISTRO_SPECS or /etc/puppyversion), hover preview launches
  `run-as-spot mpv ...`. If run-as-spot is missing, preview is skipped instead
  of running mpv as root.
- On non-Puppy systems, and when Puppy itself is already running ROX as a
  non-root user, audio preview launches mpv normally.
- Audio preview runs in its own process group, so leaving the file stops the
  complete run-as-spot/su/mpv chain without touching unrelated mpv instances.
- Keeps the same one-second hover delay and audio/* MIME support from 2.12.2-6.
- Fixes the 2.12.2-6 build failure in filer.c by including debug_log.h for ROX_LOG_DEBUG.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-6 (2026-08-13)

- Added optional video thumbnails in Options > Thumbnails. When enabled,
  Rox-Filer2 uses ffmpeg directly, first trying a frame at 10 seconds and
  falling back to 1 second for short clips. No ffmpegthumbnailer dependency.
- Added audio hover preview with mpv, enabled by default. Resting the pointer
  on audio/* files for one second starts audio-only playback; moving away
  stops only the mpv PID started by Rox-Filer2.
- Kept Browser command visible in Options > Desktop > Browser and Console,
  including support for %u and the defaultbrowser/x-www-browser/
  gnome-www-browser/xdg-open fallback chain.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-5 (2026-08-13)

- Fixes the desktop browser build by exposing rox_open_browser() to desktop.c.
- Moves Trash handling out of the forked action child; this avoids a GTK/GLib
  GIO deadlock that could leave the Move to Trash operation hanging forever.
- Fixes the signedness warning when checking whether a directory item is Home.
- Adds one central browser launcher, rox_open_browser(), used by the built-in
  desktop Browser icon.
- Browser command is configurable from Options -> Desktop; %u is replaced by
  the requested URL.
- With no custom browser, tries defaultbrowser, x-www-browser and
  gnome-www-browser with --new-tab, retries each wrapper without --new-tab if
  it exits immediately with an error, and uses xdg-open only as the last
  fallback.
- Console/terminal selection is automatic when no command is configured:
  defaultterminal, x-terminal-emulator, xterm, then urxvt.
- The same terminal selection is shared by the desktop Console icon, Open
  Terminal Here and Run in Terminal.
- Browser and Console command fields now live together in Options -> Desktop,
  beside the built-in desktop controls.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-4 (2026-08-09)

- X11/XLibre file context menus are now built from a fresh GtkMenu/GtkMenuItem
  tree for every right-click instead of reusing a mutable menu for the whole
  Rox-Filer2 session.
- MIME/XDG and AppMenu entries belong only to that popup and are removed before
  the complete transient context menu is destroyed.
- Removes the manual PRELIGHT/SELECTED/ACTIVE/FOCUSED state-flag clearing
  introduced during earlier diagnosis and lets GtkMenuShell manage normal menu
  state again.
- Desktop, wbar, toolbar, MIME cache and file-operation code are unchanged from
  2.12.2-3.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-3 (2026-08-09)

- Environment refreshes are now geometry-only and preserve the existing
  desktop widgets instead of rebuilding the complete icon layer.
- Unrelated desktop.conf writes no longer reload an unchanged wallpaper or
  restart wbar on X11/XLibre.
- A real wallpaper path/style change still updates the wallpaper and wbar;
  the follow-up environment refresh only recalculates desktop geometry.
- Keeps the 2.12.2-2 desktop selection/hover/focus cleanup unchanged.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-2 (2026-08-09)

- X11/XLibre desktop activation now releases desktop selection, hover and
  keyboard focus after opening an item, preventing stale GTK3 desktop state
  from leaking into later filer popup-menu rendering.
- No contextual-menu implementation changes in this build; this release is a
  focused test/fix for the desktop-to-filer state transition.

Rox-Filer2 2.12.2-1 (2026-08-09)

- Consolidates the tested development work after the public 2.12-r82 release
  into a new clean release version.
- Keeps the GTK3 MIME icon RAM cache so system-theme MIME icons are not
  repeatedly reloaded every few seconds.
- Adds built-in Home, Browser, Console and Trash desktop icons, configurable
  from Options -> Desktop and resolved from the active system icon theme.
- Keeps Home first among built-in desktop icons when it is enabled.
- Adds the compact text-under-icons toolbar, persistent filer icon size and
  unified desktop hover feedback.
- Uses a single item context menu, direct Bookmarks access and Add to
  Bookmarks for directories.
- Adds Restore / Restore Selected inside the Freedesktop Trash view and hides
  Move to Trash while already browsing Trash.
- Fast Copy, Move, Link, Trash and permanent-delete operations no longer flash
  a progress window when they finish in under 500 ms.
- X11/XLibre context menus use a real root GtkMenu and clear stale visual
  selection state before popup.
- The terminal emulator is configurable through Rox-Filer2 Options and is now
  shared by Open Terminal Here, Run in Terminal and the desktop Console icon.
  New configurations default to xterm.
- X11/XLibre and native Wayland/Labwc desktop backends remain supported.

Rox-Filer2 2.12-r82 (2026-08-08)

- Fixed the invalid GtkTextTag `weight` vararg in the action dialog. Passing
  the string "bold" to an integer GObject property produced random negative
  values and GLib-GObject errors; it now uses PANGO_WEIGHT_BOLD.
- Fixed the intermittent `g_spawn_sync(): ECHILD` warning during asynchronous
  desktop drive scans by serializing synchronous child waits against ROX's
  legacy SIGCHLD/waitpid(-1) reaper.
- Removed Rox-Filer2's explicit unsetenv("APP_DIR") call. APP_DIR is retained
  rather than modifying the process environment after GLib initialization.
- Kept the r81 Wayland Copy/Move/Link chooser and Refresh Desktop grid
  organization unchanged.

Rox-Filer2 2.12-r81 (2026-08-08)

- Wayland DND: preserve the Copy/Move/Link chooser for cross-process drags
  when GTK reports no source widget but the source offered GDK_ACTION_ASK.
- Refresh Desktop now reorders desktop file/trash icons onto the normal grid
  and persists the cleaned positions, while keeping the drive area reserved.
- Built directly from the user-provided r80 tree; custom icon artwork kept.

Rox-Filer2 2.12-r80 (2026-08-08)

* Restore Cut, Copy and Paste in the quick right-click File menu.
* Wayland: emulate ROX's classic drag action chooser for internal cross-window
  drags instead of depending on compositor negotiation of GDK_ACTION_ASK.
* Add technical DND logging for drop actions and chooser decisions.
* Keep /usr/local/apps/Rox-Filer and existing configuration paths unchanged.

2026-08-08 Rox-Filer2 2.12-r79

- Corregida la apertura de ventanas normales en Wayland desde `rox`,
  `rox-wayland`, el menú y lanzadores .desktop.
- La tabla SOAP/RPC ahora se inicializa independientemente del transporte X11.
  En r78 el retorno temprano de `remote_init()` en Wayland dejaba `rpc_calls`
  en NULL y `run_soap()` fallaba con `g_hash_table_lookup: hash_table != NULL`.
- `run_soap()` inicializa defensivamente el registro RPC para rutas que omiten
  `remote_init()` (incluido el modo desktop).
- Se mantiene sin cambios la AppDir `/usr/local/apps/Rox-Filer`.

2026-08-08 Rox-Filer2 2.12-r78
- Project branding changed from ROX-Filer GTK3 to Rox-Filer2 while preserving
  the original ROX-Filer credits and compatibility configuration paths.
- Fixed native Wayland menu/AppDir launches: normal filer processes no longer
  fork after gtk_init() on Wayland, avoiding inherited libwayland connections.
- `rox` is the canonical automatic launcher; `rox-x11` and `rox-wayland` force
  their respective backends. Generic ROX-Filer/Rox-Filer2 aliases use the
  automatic selector.
- Updated About, --help, package desktop entries and translation catalogues.
- Runtime AppDir is /usr/local/apps/Rox-Filer with a compatibility symlink
  /usr/local/apps/ROX-Filer; existing user configuration remains unchanged.

2026-08-07 ROX-Filer 2.12-r76

* Fix normal filer windows launched from menus or the ROX AppDir in native
  Wayland sessions. The historical remote SOAP transport is X11-only and is
  now skipped safely on non-X11 displays.
* Install /usr/local/bin/roxfiler as the automatic session-aware launcher:
  rox-wayland on Wayland and rox-x11 on X11.
* Add /usr/bin/rox as a compatibility link to the automatic launcher.
* Install the X11 error handler only when GTK is actually using X11.

2026-08-07 ROX-Filer 2.12-r75

* MIME icons now resolve through the active GTK/Freedesktop icon theme before
  the small legacy ROX theme, fixing question-mark icons for normal files.
* Diagnostic logs record the GTK icon theme, search paths, MIME icon source,
  resolved icon name and fallback failures.
* Suppress repetitive non-error GdkPixbuf debug chatter from technical logs.
* APP_DIR is removed before GLib creates worker threads, avoiding the
  unsetenv() thread-safety warning.

2.12-r75
----------
* Añade registro técnico interno desactivado por defecto para X11 y Wayland.
* Opciones nuevas: --debug, --log-file, --log-level y --clear-logs.
* Guarda por defecto en $XDG_STATE_HOME/rox-filer o ~/.local/state/rox-filer.
* Conserva como máximo cinco registros de 2 MiB cada uno.
* Registra backend, Layer Shell, escritorio, MIME, terminal, scripts y renombrado.
* Actualiza la prueba de Labwc para recoger el log interno automáticamente.

