* Carga libgtk-layer-shell.so.0 dinámicamente para no afectar X11.

ROX-Filer 2.12-r72 (2026-08-05)

- Run in Terminal now changes explicitly to the script directory before execution, so scripts using relative files work with every terminal emulator.
- Shell scripts without a shebang use the session shell, then Bash, then /bin/sh; executable text files no longer fail with ENOEXEC merely because they have no extension.
- Added opt-in ROX_DEBUG_LOG tracing for XDG application launches and terminal commands.
- Diagnostic 1.5 fixes false Open With failures caused by equivalent /tmp and /initrd paths, tests the real configured terminal, and detects stale ROX processes after upgrades.

ROX-Filer 2.12-r71 (2026-08-05)

- Fixed Run in Terminal so .bash files without a shebang use Bash instead of /bin/sh.
- Added fallback interpreters for .ash, .dash, .zsh, .ksh, .fish, Perl, Ruby, Lua, Tcl, PHP, JavaScript, AWK and sed scripts.
- A valid #! line remains authoritative and its interpreter is checked before launch.
- Restored standards-first XDG launching: GIO now receives a graphical launch context, with direct Exec= expansion only as a fallback.
- Rename dialogs are transient for the active filer window and explicitly presented, preventing them from opening behind the filer.
- Added hidden rename-dialog diagnostics and expanded the bundled diagnostic script to version 1.4.

ROX-Filer 2.12-r70 (2026-08-05)

* Open With: local .desktop files now launch their Exec= command directly before falling back to GIO, avoiding false-success D-Bus activations that open nothing.
* Open With: added hidden diagnostic hooks that exercise the exact ROX launcher with paths containing spaces and Unicode.
* Terminal: executable scripts with a shebang are parsed through their declared interpreter instead of being launched blindly by the kernel.
* Terminal: supports CRLF shebang lines, UTF-8 BOMs and /usr/bin/env -S interpreter arguments.
* Terminal: added exact diagnostic tests for executable shell scripts, non-executable shell scripts, Python scripts and CRLF shebangs.
* Diagnostics: version 1.3 records the selected MIME application, desktop Exec= line, terminal command, execution mode, arguments and child result.
* Diagnostics: optional --test-script and --geany-file arguments reproduce user-supplied failing cases in the log.

ROX-Filer 2.12-r69 (2026-08-05)

* Toolbar: replaced the two ambiguous Size buttons with explicit Smaller Icons, Automatic and Bigger Icons controls.
* Toolbar: added a dedicated Zoom Out button; reducing icon size no longer depends on a hidden secondary click.
* Terminal: chooses defaultterminal or x-terminal-emulator before falling back to xterm on new configurations.
* Terminal: parses the configured emulator directly and uses the correct command separator for common terminals.
* Terminal: Run in Terminal now launches a temporary executable runner, improving compatibility with emulators whose -e option accepts only one command.
* Terminal: extensionless and uncommon non-executable scripts with a shebang are now recognised.

ROX-Filer 2.12-r68 (2026-08-05)

* Menú contextual: Cortar, Copiar y Pegar aparecen juntos en el nivel principal.
* Cortar conserva Ctrl+X y el formato estándar x-special/gnome-copied-files.
* Pegar ya no depende de una posición numérica fija dentro del menú.
* MIME: se evita consultar fstab_mounts antes de su inicialización al usar -m.
* Diagnóstico: actualizado para separar stdout y stderr de la prueba MIME.

ROX-Filer 2.12-r67 (2026-08-05)

- Added the private `desktop-backend.h` interface and backend selector.
- Moved the X11 desktop instance property, refresh ClientMessage handling,
  EWMH desktop-window hints and X11 stacking code into `desktop-x11.c`.
- Kept wallpaper, icons, positions, menus, drives and monitor coordination in
  the common `desktop.c` module.
- Preserved the existing GTK fallback when the current display has no native
  desktop backend yet, preparing a later `desktop-wayland.c` implementation.
- Kept the public startup command unchanged: `rox --desktop`.

ROX-Filer 2.12-r66 (2026-08-05)

- Made `desktop.c`/`desktop.h` the only compiled desktop implementation.
- Removed the dormant classic `pinboard.c` backend and its pinboard task-list
  implementation from the source and build.
- Removed legacy pinboard gesture contexts and pinboard-only drag-and-drop code.
- Routed legacy ROX panels through `desktop_get_gdk_window()` so they stack
  above the single `rox --desktop` window without depending on pinboard code.
- Screen geometry changes now refresh the unified desktop module directly.

2.12-r65 (2026-08-05)

- Purged the obsolete `-p`, `--pinboard`, `-S` and `--rox-session` help
  records from every source translation catalogue.
- Regenerated all bundled GNU gettext `.mo` files so no locale can expose
  removed pinboard switches through `ROX-Filer --help`.
- Confirmed that command-line parsing accepts only `--desktop` for starting
  the ROX desktop; `-p` and `--pinboard` are not present in the short or long
  option tables.

2.12-r64 (2026-08-05)

- Made `ROX-Filer --desktop` the only public command that starts a ROX
  desktop. The named classic pinboard options `-p` and `--pinboard` were
  removed from command-line parsing and help.
- Removed `-S` and `--rox-session`, which could still activate the classic
  named pinboard indirectly.
- Removed the classic Pinboard, PinboardAdd, PinboardRemove, SetBackdrop and
  SetBackdropApp SOAP endpoints so external RPC cannot reactivate the old
  desktop implementation.
- Replaced the AppDir menu's Enable/Disable pinboard entries with one
  Start ROX Desktop action.
- Made repeated `--desktop` launches refresh the already-running X11/XLibre
  desktop and exit instead of creating a second desktop window.
- Removed classic pinboard controls from the Options window. Classic panel
  compatibility remains available during the transition.
- Kept the old pinboard source internally for now so it can be removed in
  smaller, reviewable steps without destabilising unrelated filer code.

2.12-r63 (2026-08-04)

- Fixed folder MIME detection so real directories and links to directories are
  always handled as the exact Freedesktop type inode/directory.
- Filtered the folder application list against the applications' current
  desktop files. Programs such as Geany no longer appear for a directory unless
  they explicitly declare MimeType=inode/directory.
- Fixed GTK3 double-click tracking. The first complete double click now opens
  the selected item instead of being discarded and requiring a second double
  click.
- Reserved the active GTK3 theme's user-home icon for the user's home
  directory. In Puppy this means /root is shown as user-home even when
  /root/.DirIcon or a GlobIcons association exists.
- Applied the same rule to the filer window icon while browsing the home
  directory. Other directories continue to support .DirIcon normally.
- Added a direct Desktop Entry Exec= fallback when GIO cannot launch a MIME
  application, especially on Puppy installations without working D-Bus
  activation.
- Expanded standard Desktop Entry field codes including %f, %F, %u, %U, %i,
  %c, %k and %% so applications with more complex Exec= lines can open files.
- Fixed undefined varargs reads in the .desktop parser, which could make some
  application entries behave unpredictably.
- When both launch methods fail, ROX-Filer now returns to the application
  chooser instead of consuming the click without opening the selected file.

2.12-r61 (2026-08-04)

- Synchronized the maintained ROX-Filer catalogues against one master set of
  1,461 active interface messages.
- Added translations for all 279 GTK3 strings introduced by the new
  desktop, paired-window, search, MIME association and file-action features in
  Arabic, Catalan, German, Spanish, French, Hungarian, Italian, Japanese,
  Portuguese, Russian, Simplified Chinese and Traditional Chinese.
- Completed the remaining untranslated Spanish entries.
- Removed fuzzy markers from the maintained catalogues and regenerated every
  bundled GNU gettext .mo file.
- Added pt and zh locale aliases and a translation coverage report.
- Added a current messages.pot template so future translations begin from the
  same source catalogue.
- Historical upstream strings without a native translation remain visible in
  English instead of becoming blank or disappearing from the interface.

2.12-r60 (2026-08-04)

- Replaced the empty Open With branch with a reliable Open With command that
  always opens the complete XDG application chooser.
- Added a custom GTK3 chooser which lists MIME-compatible applications first
  and then all installed applications, including direct scans of the real XDG
  application directories when mimeinfo.cache is incomplete.
- Kept Add Custom Application available from the chooser so a user can enter a
  command when no installed application is suitable.
- Recognised directories as inode/directory for MIME applications and custom
  actions instead of excluding folders from the modern association system.
- Moved Search in This Folder to the top of the selected-folder menu and changed
  its menu icon to the normal small edit-find icon.
- Kept MIME applications and matching custom actions visible directly at the
  beginning of the contextual menu.
- Added a direct Add File Action entry for the current file or directory; its
  manager remains beside MIME associations in Options.
- Updated the Spanish catalogue for the corrected chooser and menu labels.

2.12-r59 (2026-08-03)

- Restored the classic ROX MIME-tools workflow: applications associated with a
  selected file are shown directly at the top of the contextual File menu.
- Kept the modern XDG/GIO backend while adding a fallback scanner for actual
  .desktop files in the user and system application directories. This makes
  Open With useful on Puppy and other small distributions even when
  mimeinfo.cache is missing or outdated.
- Open With now lists the default, recommended, registered and desktop-declared
  applications without depending only on the GIO recommendation cache.
- Matching user file actions are displayed beside the MIME applications rather
  than being hidden inside a separate empty Custom Actions submenu.
- Added Add File Action, Manage Applications and Manage File Actions entries to
  the Open With menu. New actions opened from a selection are pre-filled with
  the current MIME type and target kind.
- Merged File Associations and Custom Actions into one Options page named
  MIME Types and File Actions, with direct Add Application and Add File Action
  buttons plus both managers in the same place.
- Removed the separate Custom Actions branch from the contextual menu.
- Continued to ignore legacy OpenWith and SendTo directories without deleting
  any existing user data.
- Updated the Spanish catalogue for the new foreground MIME and file-action UI.

2.12-r58 (2026-08-03)

- Removed the active use of the historical ROX OpenWith and SendTo directories.
  Existing directories are left untouched but are no longer read by the filer.
- Replaced the file Open With menu with applications provided by GIO and the
  standard XDG desktop application database.
- Added Choose Another Application with an optional remember-as-default control.
- Files without a default association now open the GTK application chooser directly;
  the same dialog also offers Add Custom Application.
- Added Add Custom Application for creating user .desktop launchers below the
  active user's XDG data directory.
- Added a GTK3 icon chooser with SVG, PNG, JPEG, WebP and XPM previews. Selected
  icons are copied into the active user's hicolor icon tree so removable source
  paths are not retained.
- Added management of ROX-created custom applications from the Options window.
- Added modern Custom Actions as a replacement for legacy SendTo entries. Actions
  can target files, directories or symbolic links and can be limited by MIME
  type and single or multiple selection.
- Added a Custom Actions manager with Add, Edit, Remove and Enable controls.
- Custom action commands are validated before their desktop-entry files are saved.
- Changed the default right-click behaviour so selected files and directories
  show their contextual actions directly; the general ROX menu remains available
  on empty space or with the Control modifier.
- Kept all user paths distribution-independent through GLib XDG functions; no
  /root or fixed /home path is used by the new modules.
- Added new XDG application and Custom Actions pages to the rebuilt Options GUI.

Build fix
---------
- Include main.h and support.h in filer_pair.c so the paired-window module has declarations for home_dir and pathdup.

2.12-r57 (2026-08-02)

- Reorganised the GTK3 Options window into modern General, Navigation and
  Clicks, View, Thumbnails, Paired Windows, Search, File Operations, Toolbar,
  Desktop and Classic Compatibility pages.
- Added an optional directory-only single-click mode. Files and AppDirs keep
  the double-click behaviour when this mode is active.
- Added native paired ROX-Filer windows without wmctrl, xprop, Xdialog or
  external window-management scripts. The feature supports left/right and
  top/bottom layouts, configurable split and gap, remembered directories,
  menu and toolbar actions, and --pair / --pair-realign commands.
- Added ROX File Search as a separate C/GTK3 binary named rox-find. It follows
  the active GTK theme and uses the supplied rox-find application icon.
- Integrated Search in This Folder and Search in Selected Folders into the
  ROX contextual menu, plus an optional Search toolbar action.
- Added recursive name and glob search, hidden-file, case, type, size,
  symbolic-link and filesystem controls, optional text-content search with a
  configurable maximum file size, cancellation and progressively displayed
  results.
- Added result actions for Open, Show in ROX-Filer, Open Parent Folder, Copy
  Path and Move to Trash.
- Added rox-find.desktop and Arabic, Catalan, German, Spanish, French,
  Hungarian, Italian, Japanese, Portuguese, Russian and Chinese catalogues.
- Added the real ROX-Filer --desktop-refresh command. It sends an X11 client
  message to the already-running ROX Desktop and refreshes desktop files,
  Trash, devices, work area and icon placement without starting a second
  desktop process.
- Made the legacy SendTo directory menu optional and disabled by default. XDG
  application menus remain available. Native terminal actions are hidden when
  they do not apply instead of remaining as disabled clutter.
- Moved thumbnail storage to the Freedesktop cache location under
  ~/.cache/thumbnails/normal and updated cache purging accordingly.
- Added configurable Recently Visited history length and optional filtering of
  directories that no longer exist.
- Preserved broken symbolic links in normal filer views so accidental target
  deletion remains visible to the user.
- Added the rox-find binary, desktop entry, application icons and translations
  to Debian and portable package output.
- Improved paired-window layout on small monitor work areas and prevented the
  normal filer minimum geometry from forcing the paired windows to overlap.
- Improved ROX File Search shutdown so closing the window cancels an active
  search safely and exits after its worker finishes.
- Updated Debian dependency metadata to accept both current t64 GTK/GLib
  runtime package names and their older compatible names.
- Fixed a leaked resolved path in filer_close_recursive().
- Fixed ownership handling for the parent array returned by
  xdg_mime_list_mime_parents() by using free() instead of g_strfreev().

