  on the names commonly available in Puppy icon themes: `drive-removable-media`
  for USB/removable drives, `media-cdrw` for optical drives such as `sr0`, and
  `media-flash` for SD/MMC cards.
- More specific Freedesktop, GNOME and Puppy icon names remain as secondary
  fallbacks. `drive-harddisk` is still restricted to the final fallback and is
  never preferred for USB, optical or flash media.

ROX-Filer 2.12 GTK3 - ROX Desktop r33 - 2026-07-28
---------------------------------------------------------

- Modificado por josejp2424 (2026): corrected the final drive-icon resolver.
  USB, SD/MMC, optical (including sr0), floppy, SSD/NVMe, network and internal
  units now keep their semantic icon order instead of moving drive-harddisk to
  the front whenever the active GTK theme lacks a specific name.
- ROX now mirrors EssoraWM's fallback search through Puppy pixmap directories
  and all installed icon themes. An incomplete custom theme can no longer make
  a USB stick or optical drive appear as an internal hard disk.
- Added symbolic and legacy Puppy/GNOME icon-name fallbacks while preserving
  the selected icon theme whenever it provides the correct device icon.

ROX-Filer 2.12 GTK3 - ROX Desktop r32 - 2026-07-28
---------------------------------------------------------

- Modificado por josejp2424 (2026): removed the global map-time
  `GTK_WIN_POS_CENTER_ALWAYS` hook introduced with the operation dialogs.
  Dialogs are centred before being shown, avoiding repeated window-manager
  geometry negotiations that delayed right-click menus.
- Copy, move, Trash and Delete GIFs now stop and are released when the
  operation finishes, so completed dialogs do not continue repainting.
- ROX Desktop drive scans now run in a worker thread. The periodic
  `lsblk`/sysfs scan no longer blocks GTK's main loop or delays the desktop
  context menu. Desktop-folder changes no longer trigger a drive rescan.
- Partitions inherit transport, removable, model, optical and rotational data
  from their physical parent through `lsblk PKNAME` and sysfs. This fixes USB
  partitions whose own `TRAN` field is empty.
- ROX Desktop and the Partitions GUI now call the same icon function. It first
  uses the icon supplied by GIO when available, then resolves USB, SD/MMC,
  optical, SSD/NVMe, network and internal fallback names from the active GTK
  icon theme.
- Agregado por josejp2424 (2026): on X11, wallpaper changes also update the
  root pixmap through hsetroot, feh or xwallpaper. When wbar is already
  running, ROX performs the EssoraWM-style verified refresh asynchronously:
  stop live non-zombie instances, reapply the wallpaper and start one fresh
  wbar process.

